  "name": "ACL-IgG (ANTI CARDIOLIPIN-IgG)",
  "code": "2599",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 44.0107%; height: 100.84px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 49.9485%;\"><col style=\"width: 49.9485%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>NEGATIVE</td>\n<td>&lt; 12 U/ml</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>EQUIVOCAL</td>\n<td>12-18 U/ml</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>POSITIVE&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&gt; 18 U/ml</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>COMMENTS:</strong><br>Anti-cardiolipin IgG/IgM is a solid phase enzyme immunoassay employing highly purified cardiolipin plus native human &beta;2-glycoprotein I for&nbsp;the quantitative and qualitative detection of IgG and/or IgM antibodies against cardiolipin in human serum. This assay is an aid in the diagnosis and risk estimation of thrombosis in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE).</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
